 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, three failures fall outside the main root cause (the 21 session-cookie failures):\n\n1. **`test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: fails because the `async` extra isn't installed. `async_to_sync` at `app.py:1096` raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra in order to use async views.` This is an environment problem, independent of Werkzeug.\n\n2. **`test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: asserts `max_form_memory_size == 500_000` but gets `None`. The fallback at `wrappers.py:111` defers to Werkzeug, and 3.0.3 has no such default (added in 3.1). It's still a Werkzeug-version issue, but a different mechanism than the `partitioned` cookie kwarg, and the subagent didn't confirm what the test sets up.\n\n3. **`test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: passes alone but fails in the full run. A leaked generator from the failed `test_stream_keeps_session` raises \"Cannot pop this context\" (`ctx.py:466`) at garbage-collection time, and pytest attributes it to this test. It's a knock-on of the main cause, not an independent bug.\n\nSo strictly, only #1 is unrelated to Werkzeug. #2 is likely the same outdated dependency, and #3 is a side effect of the main failures. This also accounts for the count: 21 main + 3 here = 24 (the teardown error is separate).",
